Legion Go: map the touchpad on new (2025+) firmware

Firmware revisions that expose the touchpad as BTN_TOUCH + BTN_0 (rather
than BTN_TOOL_FINGER + BTN_TOOL_DOUBLETAP) were not matched by hhd's Legion
Go tablet profile, so the touchpad was unusable (no cursor, no tap-to-click,
no two-finger scroll).

Teach the profile to accept BTN_TOUCH and map touchpad_left to BTN_0.

This is the change that was previously applied by hand to the installed
site-packages copy of hhd; keeping it as a patch means a rebuilt hhd keeps
the fix instead of silently reverting it.
--- a/src/hhd/device/legion_go/tablet/const.py
+++ b/src/hhd/device/legion_go/tablet/const.py
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 
 LGO_TOUCHPAD_BUTTON_MAP: dict[int, Button] = to_map(
     {
-        "touchpad_touch": [B("BTN_TOOL_FINGER")],  # also BTN_TOUCH
-        "touchpad_right": [B("BTN_TOOL_DOUBLETAP")],
+        "touchpad_touch": [B("BTN_TOUCH")],
+        "touchpad_left": [B("BTN_0")],
     }
 )
 
--- a/src/hhd/device/legion_go/tablet/base.py
+++ b/src/hhd/device/legion_go/tablet/base.py
@@ -270,7 +270,7 @@
         vid=[0x17EF],
         pid=[0x6182, 0x61EB],
         name=[re.compile(".+Touchpad")],  # "  Legion Controller for Windows  Touchpad"
-        capabilities={EC("EV_KEY"): [EC("BTN_MOUSE")]},
+        capabilities={EC("EV_KEY"): [EC("BTN_TOUCH")]},
         btn_map=LGO_TOUCHPAD_BUTTON_MAP,
         axis_map=LGO_TOUCHPAD_AXIS_MAP,
         aspect_ratio=1,
